WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.338 --> 00:00:02.946
- If you constantly try to, you know,

00:00:02.946 --> 00:00:05.241
to reach perfection at everything,

00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:07.260
you're not going to reach it,
but you're going to get close.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.678
If all I ever did was
win or lose at a game,

00:00:10.678 --> 00:00:13.683
I don't really look at my life
has a lot of significance.

00:00:13.683 --> 00:00:15.967
- He's a professional
baseball outfielder playing

00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:17.445
for the New York Mets.

00:00:17.445 --> 00:00:20.045
He's a former professional
American football player

00:00:20.045 --> 00:00:22.379
who played three seasons in the NFL.

00:00:22.379 --> 00:00:25.197
He was selected by the Denver
Broncos in the first round

00:00:25.197 --> 00:00:27.429
of the 2010 NFL draft.

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:29.218
He's Tim Tebow, and here's my take

00:00:29.218 --> 00:00:31.126
on his Top 10 Rules For Success.

00:00:31.126 --> 00:00:33.147
Rule number nine is my personal favorite

00:00:33.147 --> 00:00:35.717
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:35.717 --> 00:00:37.092
And as always as you're watching

00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:39.457
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:40.940
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.840
put quotes around it so other
people can be inspired as well

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.986
and when you write it
down it's much more likely

00:00:45.986 --> 00:00:47.961
to stick with you as well.

00:00:47.961 --> 00:00:49.009
Enjoy.

00:00:49.009 --> 00:00:51.757
(swooshing)

00:00:51.757 --> 00:00:54.340
(lively music)

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.330
- Why Baseball?

00:01:07.797 --> 00:01:11.296
- When I was four, five, six
years old it was my first love,

00:01:11.296 --> 00:01:13.021
this first thing I fell in love with

00:01:13.021 --> 00:01:15.205
and I thought most of my life

00:01:15.205 --> 00:01:18.256
I thought I was going to pursue
baseball as a profession.

00:01:18.256 --> 00:01:20.252
Second hardest decision of my life.

00:01:20.252 --> 00:01:23.162
I remember sitting on the
edge of my bed crying over it,

00:01:23.162 --> 00:01:24.254
deciding what I was going to do,

00:01:24.254 --> 00:01:27.707
and I ended up choosing football
and I don't regret that.

00:01:27.707 --> 00:01:31.301
But, I do believe in pursuing passions

00:01:31.301 --> 00:01:32.209
and what's on your heart,

00:01:32.209 --> 00:01:34.183
and this is something
that I'm passionate about.

00:01:34.183 --> 00:01:35.411
- What's it say about you

00:01:35.411 --> 00:01:38.547
that you're even given the
opportunity as a 29-year-old man

00:01:38.547 --> 00:01:40.535
who hadn't played baseball in a decade?

00:01:40.535 --> 00:01:42.758
- There's certain things
in life that we love,

00:01:42.758 --> 00:01:45.174
and we have chances to pursue 'em.

00:01:45.174 --> 00:01:48.033
But a lot of the time
the fear of the unknown,

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:49.820
the fear of failure gets in the way.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.278
I don't want that fear to creep in,

00:01:51.278 --> 00:01:52.900
I don't want the unknown to creep in.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.284
I want to be someone that I pursue

00:01:55.284 --> 00:01:57.722
whatever is on my heart
with everything I have

00:01:57.722 --> 00:01:59.754
and if I fall flat on my
face, then guess what?

00:01:59.754 --> 00:02:01.311
I'mma get right back up.

00:02:01.311 --> 00:02:03.500
- I've read that you're a farce.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.378
I've read that you're a joke.

00:02:05.378 --> 00:02:07.464
I've read that you're an embarrassment.

00:02:07.464 --> 00:02:10.667
Not only to yourself, but
to the game of baseball.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.221
- The first thing is I'm so thankful

00:02:12.221 --> 00:02:15.212
that I don't have to read it,
I don't have to listen to it.

00:02:15.212 --> 00:02:16.911
I don't have to live the rollercoaster

00:02:16.911 --> 00:02:19.233
that the rest of the
world lives of my life.

00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:20.833
I don't care what they write about me.

00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:22.190
They've written a lot of things

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:24.215
over the last 15 years about me.

00:02:24.215 --> 00:02:25.801
Some good, some not good,

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:27.578
some just 'cause they want to sell papers.

00:02:27.578 --> 00:02:29.069
I don't necessarily care.

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:31.563
At the end of the day, I
want to pursue my passion

00:02:31.563 --> 00:02:34.097
because I believe when you're
pursuing what's on your heart,

00:02:34.097 --> 00:02:36.211
when you're pursuing
what you're convicted by,

00:02:36.211 --> 00:02:37.717
then I don't have to live with the regret

00:02:37.717 --> 00:02:40.342
10, 15, 20 years from
now looking back saying,

00:02:40.342 --> 00:02:42.971
what if, what if I would have tried that?

00:02:42.971 --> 00:02:46.132
Where it's a success is
if I give my all to it.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.577
If I get to live out that
dream every single day,

00:02:48.577 --> 00:02:50.606
whether that's in Single-A,
Double-A, Triple-A,

00:02:50.606 --> 00:02:52.055
or it's in the big leagues.

00:02:52.055 --> 00:02:55.382
Because joy doesn't come from success.

00:02:55.382 --> 00:02:59.020
Joy comes from knowing your design,

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.981
and being able to pursue
that every single day,

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:05.405
and knowing that I get
to live out a dream.

