00:11:02.769 --> 00:11:04.038
to wear people down.

00:11:04.038 --> 00:11:06.452
Where I feel like I have an
advantage in the 4th quarter,

00:11:06.452 --> 00:11:07.869
and the 2nd half.

00:11:08.891 --> 00:11:11.595
And that's how I like to train,

00:11:11.595 --> 00:11:13.909
is to be able to feel like I have an edge,

00:11:13.909 --> 00:11:15.296
and I feel like that is my edge,

00:11:15.296 --> 00:11:16.976
and so I like to train that way.

00:11:16.976 --> 00:11:19.692
(lively music)

00:11:19.692 --> 00:11:21.323
You know, whatever you're doing,

00:11:21.323 --> 00:11:23.241
put everything into it, put
your whole heart into it

00:11:23.241 --> 00:11:24.759
and you're going to get
something out of it.

00:11:24.759 --> 00:11:26.737
So if you really want to become your best,

00:11:26.737 --> 00:11:28.778
push yourself in whatever you're doing

00:11:28.778 --> 00:11:31.219
as hard as you possibly can
and you will find results.

00:11:31.219 --> 00:11:33.289
It's not always about the workout,

00:11:33.289 --> 00:11:35.057
it's about the work ethic.

00:11:35.057 --> 00:11:36.517
And knowing you have the work ethic,

00:11:36.517 --> 00:11:38.561
then you can find the right
workout to fit your body

00:11:38.561 --> 00:11:41.978
and fit what you're trying to accomplish.

00:11:43.162 --> 00:11:46.079
(electronic music)

00:11:52.832 --> 00:11:54.477
- Push!

00:11:54.477 --> 00:11:55.368
- [Man] What's he doing?

00:11:55.368 --> 00:11:59.084
- [Man] He's been
pushing like since seven.

00:11:59.084 --> 00:12:00.745
- [Man] Keep pushing that!

00:12:00.745 --> 00:12:01.745
- [Man] Yes!

00:12:04.034 --> 00:12:06.617
(Tim groaning)

00:12:08.149 --> 00:12:09.482
- [Man] Game on!

00:12:14.499 --> 00:12:16.307
- See what we need to do
to get a picture of this.

00:12:16.307 --> 00:12:19.233
(music drowning out speaker)

00:12:19.233 --> 00:12:20.829
- [Woman] I'm so excited to see you!

00:12:20.829 --> 00:12:23.169
- You all have a blessed day.

00:12:23.169 --> 00:12:25.229
(electronic music)

00:12:25.229 --> 00:12:27.073
- [Man] Go! Go!

00:12:27.073 --> 00:12:29.086
- [Man] Push! Go!

00:12:29.086 --> 00:12:31.669
Already up to 10 miles an hour.

00:12:35.704 --> 00:12:38.454
- [Man] Back there at that point.

00:12:42.102 --> 00:12:44.519
- [Man] Going to need a ride?

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:49.225
- [Man] Go on and get a ride there, boy.

00:12:49.225 --> 00:12:52.142
(electronic music)

00:13:07.425 --> 00:13:09.416
- My philosophy since I was a little boy

00:13:09.416 --> 00:13:12.208
is hard work beats talent, when
talent doesn't work as hard.

00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:14.986
I think the biggest example
is just how I go about

00:13:14.986 --> 00:13:17.359
living every day and honestly practicing.

00:13:17.359 --> 00:13:19.817
And when people say, why
do you practice so hard?

00:13:19.817 --> 00:13:21.475
Or, why do you run every sprint so hard?

00:13:21.475 --> 00:13:23.822
You don't have to do it,
you're in good enough shape.

00:13:23.822 --> 00:13:25.341
Well it's not just because I'm doing it

00:13:25.341 --> 00:13:27.727
to get in better shape or
I'm doing it to be a leader.

00:13:27.727 --> 00:13:30.420
No I'm doing it because
everything I do I want to,

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:33.746
you know, set the mark that
this is how you know, I do it.

00:13:33.746 --> 00:13:35.743
Because I do all things
for the glory of God.

00:13:35.743 --> 00:13:38.031
I do everything as hard
as I can because I do want

00:13:38.031 --> 00:13:39.192
to set a good example.

00:13:39.192 --> 00:13:40.449
Because I do want to be a good leader.

00:13:40.449 --> 00:13:41.831
Because I do want to be in shape.

00:13:41.831 --> 00:13:43.357
Because I do want to
be the hardest worker.

00:13:43.357 --> 00:13:45.927
But more than anything,
because when I do something,

00:13:45.927 --> 00:13:48.678
I want to be the best
that I possibly can at it.

00:13:48.678 --> 00:13:49.628
Get in here!

00:13:49.628 --> 00:13:50.461
Hey!

00:13:50.461 --> 00:13:53.503
We got 30 minutes to worry
about the rest of our lives!

00:13:53.503 --> 00:13:56.154
30 minutes for the rest of our lives!

00:13:56.154 --> 00:13:57.570
There's nowhere better than first now!

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.525
It ain't happening!

00:13:58.525 --> 00:14:00.196
We get the ball, I promise you one thing.

00:14:00.196 --> 00:14:01.314
We're going to hit somebody,

00:14:01.314 --> 00:14:03.149
and we're taking it
downfield for a touchdown.

00:14:03.149 --> 00:14:04.329
I guarantee you that!

00:14:04.329 --> 00:14:05.311
- [Player] It's guaranteed.

00:14:05.311 --> 00:14:06.665
- Look at me!

00:14:06.665 --> 00:14:08.241
Look at me!

00:14:08.241 --> 00:14:12.124
We've got 30 minutes for
the rest of our lives!

00:14:12.124 --> 00:14:13.015
Let's go!

00:14:13.015 --> 00:14:14.681
- Let's go!

00:14:14.681 --> 00:14:16.053
Hey, hey, hey!

00:14:16.053 --> 00:14:18.207
(shouting)

00:14:18.207 --> 00:14:19.400
Put your heart on the table.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.251
(shouting)

00:14:21.251 --> 00:14:24.084
(uplifting music)

00:14:47.588 --> 00:14:49.041
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:49.041 --> 00:14:52.097
I made this video because
Hector Sanchez asked me to.

00:14:52.097 --> 00:14:55.005
Also if you want to nominate
someone for the next top 10 video

00:14:55.005 --> 00:14:57.454
please check the description
for a link to a video

00:14:57.454 --> 00:14:58.878
where you can vote for people

00:14:58.878 --> 00:15:00.747
and put in your suggestions as well.

00:15:00.747 --> 00:15:03.021
I'd love to know, what did
you take from this video?

00:15:03.021 --> 00:15:06.006
What was the most important
lesson that you learned

00:15:06.006 --> 00:15:09.168
that blew your mind that you're
going to immediately apply

00:15:09.168 --> 00:15:11.266
to your life or your business somehow?

00:15:11.266 --> 00:15:12.908
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:15:12.908 --> 00:15:14.314
I'm super curious to find out.

00:15:14.314 --> 00:15:16.314
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Mike Markham

00:15:16.314 --> 00:15:18.099
from restaurant-hr.com.

00:15:18.099 --> 00:15:19.935
Mike, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:15:19.935 --> 00:15:21.528
of my book Your One Word.

00:15:21.528 --> 00:15:22.964
I really appreciate the support

00:15:22.964 --> 00:15:24.393
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:15:24.393 --> 00:15:26.461
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:15:26.461 --> 00:15:27.734
I believe in you.

00:15:27.734 --> 00:15:29.688
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:15:29.688 --> 00:15:31.981
and whatever your one word is.

00:15:31.981 --> 00:15:34.447
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:15:34.447 --> 00:15:36.864
(swooshing)

00:15:40.485 --> 00:15:42.517
- I think whoever you are,

00:15:42.517 --> 00:15:46.250
you can at least respect
that I have an opinion on it

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:48.829
and that I believe in something

00:15:48.829 --> 00:15:51.052
and that I'm going to stand
up for what I believe.

00:15:51.052 --> 00:15:52.947
And so that's something
that I'm taking pride in

00:15:52.947 --> 00:15:55.001
is that I'm standing up
for what I believe in

00:15:55.001 --> 00:15:57.137
and I'm showing conviction
about something.

00:15:57.137 --> 00:15:59.136
And for me that's big.

00:15:59.136 --> 00:16:01.961
Most people don't wake up
every single day excited

00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:03.059
to take on life.

00:16:03.059 --> 00:16:06.589
Excited to take on the
challenges, and ready and able

00:16:06.589 --> 00:16:09.339
for whatever life throws at them.

00:16:11.679 --> 00:16:13.368
No, it's they have to have a coffee.

00:16:13.368 --> 00:16:14.989
And, you know, I got
to figure it out first

00:16:14.989 --> 00:16:17.239
then I'm going to get excited.

00:16:19.443 --> 00:16:21.267
Are you actually passionate
about what you do?

00:16:21.267 --> 00:16:24.420
Are you willing to sacrifice for it?

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.087
Are you really excited about it?

00:16:28.584 --> 00:16:30.849
Do you really love it?

00:16:30.849 --> 00:16:33.419
Do you really love it?

00:16:33.419 --> 00:16:35.066
'Cause I'll tell you this.

00:16:35.066 --> 00:16:37.738
If you do, you will have such an edge.

00:16:37.738 --> 00:16:40.036
Because people will want to be around you.

00:16:40.036 --> 00:16:40.869
Why?

00:16:40.869 --> 00:16:42.805
'Cause not many people live like that.

00:16:42.805 --> 00:16:44.927
There's just not many
people who live like that.

00:16:44.927 --> 00:16:46.950
There's not really that many people

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.630
that wake up every single day

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.704
and say, man I love life,
I'm passionate about it.

00:16:50.704 --> 00:16:52.108
I'm ready to take it on.

00:16:52.108 --> 00:16:55.094
I'm going to sacrifice for it.

00:16:55.094 --> 00:16:56.421
You don't get that a lot.

00:16:56.421 --> 00:17:00.074
But you can be that
person, do you know why?

00:17:00.074 --> 00:17:03.194
Because it's not a gift, it's a choice.

00:17:03.194 --> 00:17:04.077
That's a choice.

00:17:04.077 --> 00:17:06.454
You wake up every day, and you can say

00:17:06.454 --> 00:17:08.936
today I'm waking up to get better.

00:17:08.936 --> 00:17:10.123
I'm not waking up to get by.

00:17:10.123 --> 00:17:12.513
Today I'm waking up because I love it,

00:17:12.513 --> 00:17:14.656
I'm excited about it,
I'm passionate about it,

00:17:14.656 --> 00:17:16.760
I'm willing to sacrifice today.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.610
I'm willing to go all-in today.

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:20.908
The way that I have to train
for baseball is different

00:17:20.908 --> 00:17:22.680
than I did for so many years for football,

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.443
and taking 11, 12 years off of baseball,

00:17:26.443 --> 00:17:28.453
of off baseball, and playing football

00:17:28.453 --> 00:17:30.105
I definitely have to play
a little bit of catch-up.

00:17:30.105 --> 00:17:33.744
But it's also fun when I'm
getting to live out two dreams.

00:17:33.744 --> 00:17:36.271
- I think we all think if
you're not a certain age

00:17:36.271 --> 00:17:38.228
that you have to give
up on certain dreams,

00:17:38.228 --> 00:17:40.995
or you can't try something
new or change your direction.

00:17:40.995 --> 00:17:42.263
That's another great lesson.

00:17:42.263 --> 00:17:43.096
- Absolutely.

00:17:43.096 --> 00:17:45.859
And then also a thing is people

00:17:45.859 --> 00:17:48.354
do something based on the
chances they have of succeeding.

00:17:48.354 --> 00:17:50.984
Since when were dreams
based on the chances?

00:17:50.984 --> 00:17:53.020
Dreams are based on something
that's placed in your heart.

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:53.856
- That's right.
- And it's not based on the

00:17:53.856 --> 00:17:55.212
chances of succeeding, it's going

00:17:55.212 --> 00:17:56.408
out and living everyday.
- You have to have vision.

00:17:56.408 --> 00:17:57.491
That's right.

